00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.030
Super Quick Classic Who Explainer:

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:45.899
Doctor Who as a series has been around for
over 50 years, it started back in the 1960s

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:50.550
and ran till it was cancelled in the mid to
late 90s. Eventually Russell T Davies helped

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:55.670
the BBC reboot the series in 2005. So everything
before the reboot is referred to as Classic

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:56.180
Who.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.140
When you search for Classic episodes on Hulu,
Netflix and other streaming services it’s

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:06.100
usually listed as Classic Doctor Who, when
you just search for “Doctor Who” it usually

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.500
just returns results for the new reboot episodes.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:18.500
Right now on Hulu there are 413 listed episodes
of Classic Doctor Who, that is a shitload

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.960
of tv. That’s not all of it though, a lot
of the older episodes are missing. As of right

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.170
now there are about 800 total episodes if
you include the new reboot stuff.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:32.869
One of the big questions is “Do I have to
watch everything to understand?”, the short

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:37.220
answer is no. But watching classic episodes
will give you more context for the way Peter

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:40.369
Capaldi’s episodes play out visually and
thematically.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:43.869
Because the general sense I’ve gotten from
Capaldi is that his performance leans closest

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.860
to the third and fourth doctor’s Jon Pertwee
and Tom Baker. I’ll start with those episodes.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:51.950
But generally it’s a lot of fun to watch
the first appearance of important monsters

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.369
and villains.

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:56.979
So I’ll explain why I think each of these
episodes is important and the logic how I

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:57.619
ordered it.

00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:01.009
Starting off with the Third Doctor - He was
Capaldi’s introduction to the series. He

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:03.619
even got to visit him on the set as a child.

00:02:03.619 --> 00:02:08.310
I’ll try to limit this to five episodes
per Doctor. But there’s Spearhead from Space.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.590
It’s the first episode featuring the third
doctor in his own episode. A lot of times

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.300
when a doctor regenerated. You’d see the
new doctor, but it was technically during

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.680
a finale. Spearhead from Space was the first
episode of a new series. When you search for

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:26.610
it on Hulu it’s Season 7 Episodes 1 through
4. Those are 4 separate 25 minute episodes.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:33.610
So it was a big story. It’s famous for several
reasons.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.760
It was of course the first episode of the
third doctor, it was the first Doctor Who

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.540
episode to be broadcast in color and it was
considered the beginning of the UNIT years.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.790
A period of time where UNIT as a group was
a big part of the stories. UNIT for those

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:57.790
that don’t remeber is the Unified Intelligence
Taskforce. Spearheaded by Brigadier Lethbridge-Stewart,

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.480
on the reboot his daughter Kate is head of
UNIT, which was featured heavily in the 50th

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.510
Anniversary episode.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.340
Spearhead from Space is also interesting because
it sets off the running story of the Doctor

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.810
in Exile. The Timelords, which were still
around then, exiled the Doctor to 1970s earth

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.319
for meddling with the time continuum so much.

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:19.489
The main villains were the Autons, creepy
mannequin looking replicants. The episode

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:23.580
is a good example of a really scary creepy
story that also has a lot of humor. Which

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.610
is what people are saying Capaldi’s run
is going to be like.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:31.370
There’s also a lot of Time Lord Biology
that gets explained, so for anyone who wanted

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.769
a Time Lord Biology lesson. This is a good
episode.

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:39.170
Then there’s the first appearance of the
Master in Terror of the Autons, the Roger

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:44.040
Delgado Master. This was Season 8 Episodes
1 through 4. This was the beginning of third

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.930
doctor’s second series. I know they used
the autons in the previous series opener.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.860
But the storyline introduced us to Doctor
Who’s greatest villain and from a production

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.379
standpoint it was a soft reboot of the Third
Doctor’s run.

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:59.459
They brought in new companions, new uniforms
for the UNIT characters and a new standing

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:00.409
set. That was a UNIT lab the Doctor always
had a lot of scenes in. Remember, these were

00:04:00.409 --> 00:04:00.430
the UNIT years.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.950
Usually nowadays in the new episodes the biggest
changes people talk about are new Doctor Outfits,

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.680
New TARDIS consoles and new Companions. If
you watched the 2012 christmas special with

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.540
Matt Smith, they did all three of those things.
New TARDIS design, New Doctor Costume and

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:20.339
New Companion. Well, she was a short lived
companion. Technically Clara Oswald the companion

00:04:20.339 --> 00:04:23.460
is different from Clara Oswin Oswald the almost
companion.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:27.249
Side Note: I will address the rumors about
Jenna Coleman leaving during the christmas

00:04:27.249 --> 00:04:30.039
special this year after my Classic Who recommendations.

00:04:30.039 --> 00:04:34.879
Moving On, more Third Doctor: There’s The
Daemons, that’s also season 8 episodes 21

00:04:34.879 --> 00:04:37.430
through 25. It was the last story of season
8. It brought back The Master in this supernatural

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:41.569
story. It’s a story that invokes a Devil
like character, Doctor Who has done versions

00:04:41.569 --> 00:04:46.550
of The Devil several times. I love supernatural
stories, but this episode does a good job

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:51.879
of addressing the issue of devil as a concept.
That is, differentiating powerful supernatural

00:04:51.879 --> 00:04:55.039
beings from religious labels put on them.

00:04:55.039 --> 00:04:59.909
For any Marvel fans, this is the kind of story
you might find in a Doctor Strange comic.

00:04:59.909 --> 00:05:01.879
Doctor Who tackling mythology is always a
lot of fun.

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:05.629
They might be doing something similar this
year, so keep your eyes peeled.

00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:11.229
Then my final Third Doctor Recommendation
is The Time Warrior. Season 11 Episodes 1

00:05:11.229 --> 00:05:15.580
through 4. This was the introduction of Sarah
Jane Smith, one of if not the most famous

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.439
of all Doctor Who companions. She got her
own spinoff, so let’s just agree that she’s

00:05:19.439 --> 00:05:22.389
the most famous. She’s like the Tom Baker
of Companions.

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:29.389
This was also the episode that revealed the
Doctor’s Home Planet was named Gallifrey.

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:37.259
I know it seems strange that it took 11 seasons
before Gallifrey was given a name. But whatever.

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:41.610
The episode itself is set in medieval times
and since Capaldi has a Robin Hood Robots

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.789
of Sherwood episode, it only seems appropriate
to watch Time Warrior.

00:05:44.789 --> 00:05:48.439
I’ll be really interested to see if there
are any direct references to Time Warrior

00:05:48.439 --> 00:05:51.990
in Robots of Sherwood. Be sure to watch both
episodes and see.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.999
There are some other really notable things
in the episode too. The Time Lords lift the

00:05:55.999 --> 00:06:02.999
Doctor’s exile and we meet the Sontarans,
that’s Strax’s race.

00:06:03.189 --> 00:06:10.189
Let’s jump to the Fourth Doctor’s Episodes,
Tom Baker. Peter Capaldi famously mailed fan

00:06:10.439 --> 00:06:14.330
scripts to the Doctor Who offices as a teenager.
I think he was about 15 or so. You can see

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.639
his depictions of the Fourth Doctor in his
TARDIS.

00:06:15.639 --> 00:06:18.240
Someone asked him about the stories he wrote
on the World Tour last week and Capaldi answered

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.110
that he was a little embarrassed by his 15
year old self as we all are. I think that

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:27.300
means that he won’t be doing any public
readings of his childhood Doctor Who fan fiction.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:32.949
But we can always hope. Because that would
awesome.

00:06:32.949 --> 00:06:37.649
The Fourth Doctor’s Run gets referenced
a lot because internationally it was the most

00:06:37.649 --> 00:06:41.619
popular in terms of audience size. It was
a period in time when Doctor Who’s popularity

00:06:41.619 --> 00:06:45.399
exploded more than ever.

00:06:45.399 --> 00:06:52.399
Sarah Jane continued on as his companion for
3 of his seasons. You can either consider

00:06:52.619 --> 00:06:59.179
Planet of the Spiders or Robot his first story.
Planet of the Spiders was the Third Doctor’s

00:06:59.179 --> 00:07:04.860
finale, so Robot, Season 12 episodes 1 through
4 was the fourth doctor’s first official

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:10.839
story.

00:07:10.839 --> 00:07:16.080
There are so many good Tom Baker episodes
but Genesis of the Daleks is really important.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:21.499
It’s Season 12 Episodes 11 through 16. It’s
a six part story. We learn all about where

00:07:21.499 --> 00:07:26.869
the Daleks came from and Davros, who is the
Doctor Frankenstein to the Dalek Monster.

00:07:26.869 --> 00:07:31.159
Khaled mutants are still some of the most
horrific creatures Doctor Who has ever done.

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:35.339
Genesis is a good post-apocalyptic story about
the dangers of Mutually assured destruction.

00:07:35.339 --> 00:07:39.449
Surprise Surprise that it was produced during
the mid 70s when The Cold War was still escalating

00:07:39.449 --> 00:07:43.369
between the Soviet Union and NATO countries.

00:07:43.369 --> 00:07:50.369
Then there’s Pyramids of Mars, a very cool
egyptian mythology episode. It’s Season

00:07:51.709 --> 00:07:57.279
13 episodes 9 through 12. It introduced Sutekh,
a very powerful villain. I include this pick

00:07:57.279 --> 00:08:01.169
just because Peter Capaldi has an episode
titled Mummy on the Orient Express.

00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:05.219
I’m not expecting a ton of references in
the new story, it’s the one that Foxes is

00:08:05.219 --> 00:08:09.639
starring in. She’ll be performing a song
in the episode. Which reminds me of the time

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:13.360
Kylie Minogue starred in Voyage of the Damned
the 2007 christmas special.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:17.539
There have been a lot of real life performers
and celebrities that have starred in Doctor

00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:19.959
Who.

00:08:19.959 --> 00:08:24.749
Moving on There’s Brain of Morbius it’s
Season 13 episodes 18 through 21. For some

00:08:24.749 --> 00:08:29.619
reason it’s not on Hulu, but it is on Dailymotion.
I’ll have a master Tumblr post with links

00:08:29.619 --> 00:08:33.979
to all these episodes so you can watch them
on your computer if you want.

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:37.979
Brain of Morbius is just really cool because
the doctor has a mental battle like Matt Smith

00:08:37.979 --> 00:08:43.940
did in Nightmare in Silver where the faces
of the previous doctors flash on screen. During

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:48.129
the scene in Brain of Morbius a picture of
a young version of the first doctor flashes

00:08:48.129 --> 00:08:48.440
up.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.940
So you get to see what the first doctor looked
like as a young man. It’s just a nice piece

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.079
of history.

00:08:53.079 --> 00:08:57.560
Moving along there’s Deadly Assassin, that’s
Season 14 episodes 9 through 12. It’s a

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:01.269
Gallifrey heavy story. And I think it’s
the only time he visited Gallifrey without

00:09:01.269 --> 00:09:07.029
a companion. It established the Time Lord
rules of regeneration. The Rule of 12. Everyone

00:09:07.029 --> 00:09:13.180
was a little confused when Steven Moffat rebooted
the Doctor’s regeneration cycle in the 2013

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:15.720
Christmas Special. This is the episode where
that rule came from.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:21.790
It features the Peter Pratt Master who tries
to hijack a new cycle of regenerations. Because

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:26.740
Roger Delgado died in a real life car accident,
the series cast a new actor, Peter Pratt as

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:32.920
the Master and to explain the physical change
they used a similar regeneration explanation

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.660
that Doctor Who used to explain why each Doctor
looks different.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.709
It’s really creepy but there are a lot of
cool bits of Doctor Who canon that show up

00:09:39.709 --> 00:09:42.850
like the Eye of Harmony and the seal of Rassilon.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:47.740
Moving on, there’s Logopolis, the Fourth
Doctor’s final story. It’s Season 18 episodes

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:53.149
25 through 28. It’s also not on Hulu, so
I’ll include some alternate streaming links

00:09:53.149 --> 00:09:55.209
on tumblr.

00:09:55.209 --> 00:09:58.690
This story isn’t quite as much fun as the
other Tom Baker episodes I mentioned but it’s

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:03.019
still an important one. It was the first story
to feature Anthony Ainley’s version of The

00:10:03.019 --> 00:10:07.420
Master and it was the fourth doctor’s regeneration
into the fifth doctor, Peter Davison. Remeber,

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:12.129
in real life David Tennant, the 10th Doctor
married Peter Davison’s daughter, Georgia

00:10:12.129 --> 00:10:16.920
Moffat. Making the fifth Doctor, the father
in law of the 10th Doctor. Nice doctor who

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:21.459
trivia. And Georgia herself went on to play
Jenny, the Doctor’s future daughter in the

00:10:21.459 --> 00:10:25.339
canon of the series. Very meta, very cool.

00:10:25.339 --> 00:10:29.430
So there’s a billion other really important
episodes but since I don’t want this to

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.790
turn into an hour long video I’m just going
to include essentials from the other Doctors

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.149
in my tumblr post with streaming links.

00:10:35.149 --> 00:10:40.759
If you are a big fan of classic who be sure
to write your recommendations in the comments.

00:10:40.759 --> 00:10:45.920
